Create a decision card and print its line. The body is the sections
## Context, ## Decision and ## Consequences; -m is the decision text and is
required, --context and --consequences are optional and left out when empty.

An agent's decision is proposed (ready) and a human reviewer accepts it with
'lorvik decisions accept'. A human caller records it as accepted (done) at
once, which needs the reviewer role (exit 5 otherwise); pass --proposed to
leave it for review instead. --parent puts it under an open story.
--supersedes N names the accepted decision it replaces; N is dropped as
superseded when the new one is accepted. -p global records an org-wide one.

Examples:
  lorvik decide "Use a pgx pool" -m "pgxpool, no database/sql." --context "Queue needs SKIP LOCKED." --parent 2
  lorvik decide "Use pgx v6" -m "Move to v6." --supersedes 7 --proposed

Usage
  lorvik decide <title> -m <decision> [flags]

Flags
      --consequences string   What gets easier, harder or given up
      --context string        What is being decided and what constrains it
  -h, --help                  help for decide
  -m, --message string        The decision (required; - reads stdin)
      --parent int            Parent story number
      --proposed              Leave it proposed for a reviewer even when a human records it
      --supersedes int        Accepted decision number this one replaces

Global flags
      --api-url string   Server URL (default: LORVIK_API_URL)
      --json             Output the raw API JSON
  -p, --project string   Project slug (default: LORVIK_PROJECT or .lorvik.toml)
  -Q, --quiet            Suppress the unread notice on stderr and an empty inbox
      --session string   Session label for this chat (default: LORVIK_SESSION or derived; see lorvik session)
